SOAPBOX: Terrible conditions as almost everyone has noted. My 55' 160M vertical 'T' with its ~170 in-ground radials worked well on transmit but turned out to be a dud on receive. Atmospheric and local noise levels masked many stations, so I refrained from running ... just S&P. Only worked CO, AZ, CA, UT and SK 'out west' from here in WI along with KP4 and ZF as DX. I need a better RX antenna but with -F temps and snow here, it will be unlikely that I will be able to put something together for the SSB contest. Rig: K4D to KPA1500.
